# Filled from templates/in.liquid.lammps in d-SEAMS/dseams2_repro.
# Each value is marked recovered or new in the comment above it.
#
# Recovered from that template, which hard-codes them: units real,
# atom_style atomic, pair_style sw, the mW.sw coeff line, mass 18.015,
# the 350 K melt, timestep 5 then 10, the neighbor settings, the
# minimize line, and the NPT thermostat and barostat time constants.
# mW.sw is the potential file from the same templates directory.
#
# Recovered molecule count and box: 4096 and 49.62270434822753 angstrom,
# the liquid 1e3 frame in paper/tex/figures/generate_figure_data.py.
# pack.data is a random packing at that length. The hard core of 2.4
# angstrom and generator seed 1 are the packing rule and the default
# generator seed in d-SEAMS/dseams2_repro scripts/seed_ice.py.
#
# Temperature 215 K is the temperature in the name of
# data/mW_liquid_T215_512.data in that repository. The paper does not
# print 215 next to the 4096-molecule frame, so using it here is that
# name applied at the paper's molecule count.
#
# New: pressure 1.0. The liquid template names P and does not store a
# number. In units real that number is atmospheres.
#
# New split of a recovered sum: steps_melt 1000 and steps_eq 3124.
# Their sum is 4124, the timestep field in the write_data header of
# data/mW_liquid_T215_512.data (LAMMPS 22 Jul 2025). That header does
# not say how the steps were divided.
#
# New: velocity seed 1. The template names the seed and stores no integer.
# 1 is the same integer as the packing generator default, not a logged
# velocity seed.
#
# New: the dump. The template writes a data file and no trajectory.
# One frame is written at the end of the equilibration, atom ids sorted,
# so the first frame of liquid.lammpstrj is that configuration.

